# Scan-level excludes for this repository.
#
# Note: providing this file REPLACES semgrep's built-in defaults, so the usual entries are
# repeated here explicitly rather than inherited.

node_modules/
.venv/
vendor/
dist/
build/
.git/

# The fixtures are deliberately vulnerable code that the ruleset is tested against. They
# must not be scanned as if they were application source -- but they MUST still be scanned
# by ci/scripts/test-semgrep-rules.sh, which passes them explicitly.
#
# This is why the fixtures are not in a directory called `tests/`: semgrep's DEFAULT ignore
# list skips any path containing `tests`, which silently made all rules report zero findings.
ci/semgrep/fixtures/
